Z||000000||Sarlacc||06-17-2000||10:38 AM||||Hi all,<BR>This looks like a cool place for good info, you guys seem to know your stuff.<BR>Is it possible to change to a different steering wheel on my 88 GT and still have it look good?  I would like to put on one from a 99 Grand Prix (has built-in stereo/cd controls). Will be using a Pioneer DEH-77 head unit with a Soundgate REMOTE1 interface.<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-17-2000||05:19 PM||||I would think that any steering wheel would work.  Just remember that the rear of ours is round and the rear of some (like in my wifes Cav) is rectangular.  I think that would be the only thing that would matter as far as looks are concerned.  I have no idea how you would hook up a steering wheel remote if it's wired.  Maybe you already have that figured out??||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-17-2000||05:21 PM||||BTW--Where'd you come up with your handle at??  Did you ever live on Tattooine?||||reg||1
Z||000003||84 Indy||06-17-2000||06:40 PM||||Sarlacc, You need to check out the back of the steering wheel. what you are looking for is extra copper rings Some of these wheels have wires that run to the radio that would be hooked to the remote adapter. I have not heard of anyone making an infrared steering wheel. So you might have to transplant the column. Or maybe you have an idea for a new product.<p>[This message has been edited by 84 Indy (edited 06-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||06-17-2000||08:36 PM||||Doesn't the 99 GA have an airbag too? That could also be a problem.||||reg||1
