Z||000007||Sarlacc||06-17-2000||09:11 PM||||The wheel I am referring to is probably going to be purchased from the dealership, it does not include the airbag:<P>Grapite Leather Wrap Gran Prix Steering Wheel  16756820   $449.00 <P>(anyone hooked-up with discount dealer parts?)<P>The Soundgate REMOTE1 can interface most aftermarket headunits with late model steering wheels that use the built in controls;<BR> <A HREF="http://www.soundgate.com/gm2s-rac.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.soundgate.com/gm2s-rac.html</A> <P>I was just wondering how big a pain it would be to adapt(bolts match up, etc), maybe I could use some of the trim from the column of a gran prix to make it look better?<P>Sarlacc<P>Oh yea, I used to live near there Monkey, but I got kicked out for trying to bite a princess. Bummer!<BR>  <BR>{0}{0}<BR> =VVV=<BR>              <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Sarlacc (edited 06-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||286SE'S||06-19-2000||04:09 PM||||I Installed a Pioneer SR-77 steering wheel remote control on my 86 SE with the DEH 76DH<BR>CD player. They are available at Crutchfield for about $39.00. It is great. I never have to touch the receiver, except to change CD's. The volume controls are in the back and are easy to find with fingers. It amazing how much nicer this remote makes the stereo to operate. Changing a steering wheel to get this feature seems like a lot of extra work. Oh yeah, it is removable with just a little clip release to deter theft.<BR>Terry||||reg||10
