Z||000013||Sillhouette.com||06-20-2000||09:06 PM||||The grand prix steering wheel will be too large for your fiero.  I would go with a good set of Grant 13" steering wheel so that you can get in and out of the fiero more easier and when steering you can throw tha car around more precesely (don't know how to spell sorry)   you also need a GM converter its about 50 bucks canadian.<P>Cheers||||reg||1
Z||000014||theogre||06-20-2000||10:07 PM||||before going to the dealer take a tour around the salvage yards. You may very likely find something nice for cheap that will bolt right on. There have to be at least a dozen GM parts that are direct boltup to Fiero column. I got a 4 spoke sport leather wheel in decent shape all but free from one local yard.<P>If you're bent on spending that much money I'd go after market. There are all kinds of styles available, and they will all have hardware kits available to bolt direct to the Fiero OE column. I've seen some really nice aftermarket one lately.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Sarlacc||06-21-2000||01:34 AM||||Heh thanks for all the replies guys! You know how us Fiero fanatics are, we get a wild itch to do something a certain way and nothing else will seem right.  Thought about some of the Momo models, they are real nice but I really want something with the factory type controls in the wheel.  I guess I spoil my car to much.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P><BR>Sarlacc<P>{0}{0}<BR>=VVV=<BR>||||reg||1
